---
import PageContainer from "@components/PageContainer.astro";
import BasePageLayout from "@layouts/BasePageLayout.astro";
---

<BasePageLayout title="About">
    <PageContainer>
        <h1 id="about-title" style="text-align: center;">About Me</h1>
        <div class="box">
            <h2>Experience</h2>

            <p>
                I'm experienced in software development of all kinds (systems
                programming, embedded firmware, web dev, CI/CD, game modding,
                linux sysadmin, some graphics, scripting, etc). My main
                interests are in low-level and embedded programming: C/Zig/Rust,
                microcontrollers, event loops and task switching, embedded
                device drivers, communication protocols,... all the really fun
                stuff!
            </p>
            <p>
                I also have experience in electronics of many forms, mostly
                thanks to Formula Student. Among my main interests are motor
                controllers, PCB design, power conversion, high speed digital
                and analog circuit design. I'd love for a chance to
                develop PCBs professionally.
            </p>

            <p>
                I'm always looking for exciting work opportunities. If you know
                of an opening in Embedded Systems / Firmware Development /
                Electrical Engineering or a related field, please feel free to
                reach me <a
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    href="mailto:nystromjp@gmail.com">by email</a
                >!
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
            <details open>
                <summary style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <h2 style="display: inline;">Resume</h2>
                </summary>
                <div id="resume-container">
                    <object
                        id="resume"
                        data="/Resume_Jack_Nystrom.pdf#navpanes=0&statusbar=0&messages=0&scrollbar=0&view=fit&zoom=auto"
                        type="application/pdf"
                        width="100%"
                        height="100%"
                    >
                        <p>
                            It appears your browser doesn't have PDF support.
                            You can <a href="/Resume_Jack_Nystrom.pdf"
                                >click here to download the resume PDF.</a
                            >
                        </p>
                    </object>
                    <br />
                </div>
            </details>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
            <h2>Unsorted</h2>
            A bunch of other things about me in no particular order:
            <ul>
                <li>
                    I'm a second-year undergraduate at UC Santa Cruz, studying
                    CS and EE
                </li>
                <li>
                    I spend most of my time in the basement of Baskin
                    Engineering, working on an EV racecar with <a
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        href="https://formulaslug.com/">Formula Slug</a
                    >
                </li>
                <li>
                    Passionate about my field, will talk for hours (be a nerd
                    about something, don't be boring!)
                </li>
                <li>
                    Mountain biker, but mostly as a social activity. I'm still
                    pretty mediocre tbh
                </li>
                <li>
                    You won't find me programming in anything other than Neovim
                </li>
                <li>
                    Big fan of compiled programming languages that still expose
                    the details without compromising abstractions and safety.
                    Hopeful that Zig's new IO interface and the colorless-async
                    dream will be applicable in embedded programming too
                </li>
                <li>
                    I use NixOS not because it saves me time in the long run but
                    because I absolutely love getting to control and understand
                    the pieces of my OS and the reproducibility of everything
                    down to specific program build flags and kernel parameters.
                    And because having isolated tooling is awesome
                </li>
                <li>
                    I strongly believe that cities should be designed around
                    pedestrians and bikes over the 8-lane freeways and 8ft tall
                    lifted 4x4 trucks, and people would be healthier and
                    happier. E-biking is my favorite part of the day!
                </li>
                <li>
                    I am strongly against AI. It can be a very useful tool, but
                    the way Big Tech is obsessed with it and with replacing
                    human labor is nothing short of awful. Allow me to explain.
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            The code that AI produces is mostly unuseable and/or
                            unmaintainable without skilled human review and
                            manual cleanup. In the hands of the right person
                            this can produce a viable output, but in most real
                            world cases the output of this AI-centric workflow
                            is a product with strictly worse quality and poorer
                            maintainability than the same product if it had been
                            made purely by humans. In a world where software
                            quality is essential to the everyday lives and
                            safety of billions of people, and where software is
                            already so frustratingly low-quality in so many
                            cases, I am very concerned by the direction we're
                            headed. Of course, CEOs and investors love anything
                            that promises a faster product to market. But the
                            world needs us to focus on quality, not getting out
                            the door faster.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Using an AI agent is outsourcing your intelligence
                            to a tool owned by one of ~3 billionares. We
                            sacrifice our agency and critical thinking in the
                            name of "productivity", and hand over the ownership
                            of our core product to a tool run by our greatest
                            enemies. We've introduced a link in the chain of
                            information flow with the ability to wholely
                            manipulate it in whichever way they want, invisibly
                            to the user. Furthermore, the sacrifice of our
                            learning to artificial intelligence increases our
                            dependence on it. Who does this "productivity"
                            really benefit? Hint: it's not us. (Meanwhile Nvidia
                            continues to gladly sell the shovels)
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    I am very concerned about the state of US politics, our
                    dysfunctional government, the scale of corruption, the
                    political polarization, the inability to pursue any remotely
                    radical progressive change, the intentionally mindwashing
                    media, the voter suppression, the ever-increasing national
                    debt and defense budget, the administration full of guilty
                    but unstoppable narcissists, and the embarassment of a
                    national leader
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </PageContainer>
</BasePageLayout>
<style>
    .box {
        padding: 15px;
        border-radius: 10px;
        background-color: var(--bg2);
        box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25) 0px 5px 10px;
        margin: 20px 0;
    }
    .box > p {
    }
    .box > h2 {
        margin-top: 0;
    }
    .box li {
        /* add a little vertical space between bullets */
        margin: 0.5em 0;
    }
    #about-title {
        margin: 0 10px;
        /* text-shadow: 2px 4px 9px rgba(0,0,0,0.4); */
    }
    #resume-container {
    }
    #resume {
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
        /* max-width: 40em; */
        max-width: 8.5in;
        max-height: 11in;

        aspect-ratio: 8.5 / 11;
        /* height: 11in; */
        display: block;
        border-radius: 8px;
        box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 0px 5px 10px;
        filter: brightness(85%);
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }
</style>
